2026-07-31 16:46:13,326 107423 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'task': 'bugs', 'title': "B111 CONFIRMED, OURS: image FILE artefacts are keyed on the caller's RAW string while the ledger is canonical — 4 payload directories for 2 units", 'description': "Found 2026-07-31 during image-store-sqlite Phase 1.\n\nEVIDENCE (mesh/payloads/, listed this turn): directories `!8cee336b` AND `336b` are the same\ndevice; `!987ab80f` AND `b80f` are the same device. 19 artefacts (15 .jpg, 4 .part) split across\nthe four.\n\nROOT CAUSE, exact: only ONE image call site canonicalises.\n  - mesh/lib/images.js:311  saveImageAttempt(this.resolveKey(node), ...)   <- CANONICAL\n  - mesh/lib/images.js:274  store.save(buf, { pid, ptype, node })          <- RAW\n  - mesh/lib/images.js:303  store.saveStats(node, pid, stats)              <- RAW\n  - mesh/lib/images.js:176, 209, 214, 267, 272, 273  save/load/clearPartial(node, ...) <- RAW\n  - mesh/lib/store.js:128   sub = path.join(this.dir, String(node).replace(/[^\\w!-]/g,'_'))\n\nSo the SQLite ledger is keyed correctly and every filesystem artefact is keyed on whatever the\ncaller happened to pass. store.js:192-195 already documents the consequence and works around it by\nscanning EVERY directory with a caller-supplied `match`, rather than fixing the write path.\n\nB106/B107 (e7e8492, 160a4a1) fixed the LOOKUP. The split data they were written for is still on\ndisk, and the write path that creates it is unchanged.\n\nNOT FIXED. In scope for task image-store-sqlite: any migration must canonicalise on import or it\nfaithfully reproduces the split."}
2026-07-31 16:46:20,858 107423 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_step_new args={'task': 'bugs', 'title': 'B112 CONFIRMED PRESENT / cause UNVERIFIED: image_log holds a row for unit `!8ceeb80f` — a device that does not exist', 'description': 'Found 2026-07-31 during image-store-sqlite Phase 1. Queried this turn:\n\n  !8ceeb80f  pid1  EDEADLINE  ok=0  0/0  0B  2026-07-29T06:50:15.960Z\n\n`!8cee` is the first half of `!8cee336b`; `b80f` is the second half of `!987ab80f`. It is a splice\nof the two real units and matches neither.\n\nHOW IT SURVIVED, confirmed by reading:\n  - mesh/lib/store.js:152  saveImageAttempt does `String(unit)` — no shape check, no existence check\n  - mesh/index.js:1660-1664 _unitKeySync returns the RAW string on a resolver miss. That is\n    DELIBERATE and documented ("behaviour degrades to today\'s exact-match rather than throwing"),\n    so the resolver is not splicing — it is passing an already-wrong string through.\n\nWHAT IS NOT KNOWN: which caller supplied that string. Not traced. Recording as unverified rather\nthan guessing — the value could equally have come from a manual/CLI invocation.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS BEYOND ONE ROW: a unit id that belongs to no device is permanently in the history\nany consumer reads, and nothing in the write path can reject the next one. A shape CHECK would NOT\nhave caught this value — it is well-formed. Only canonicalise-at-one-door plus an existence check\nagainst node_state would.\n\nNOT FIXED.'}
